---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How often should I measure my bra size?",
    answer: "We recommend measuring every 6 months, or whenever you experience changes in body weight, workout routines, hormonal shifts, or pregnancy. Bra sizes naturally change over time!"
  },
  {
    question: "What if my calculated size is different from what I currently wear?",
    answer: "It is extremely common to wear the wrong bra size without knowing it—studies show up to 80% of women wear incorrect sizes. Our calculator gives you an accurate baseline according to current standards."
  },
  {
    question: "What are 'Sister Sizes' and how do I use them?",
    answer: "Sister sizes share the same cup volume but have different band sizes. For example, 34C, 32D, and 36B hold the same cup volume. If a 34C band feels too loose, try 32D; if it feels too tight, try 36B."
  },
  {
    question: "Should I wear a bra when measuring?",
    answer: "Yes, measure while wearing an unlined, non-padded, lightly supported bra. Avoid padded or push-up bras as they add artificial bulk, and avoid measuring over thick clothing."
  },
  {
    question: "How should a well-fitting bra actually feel?",
    answer: "The band should sit level across your back without riding up or digging in (providing 80% of the support). The center gore (bridge) should lie flat against your breastbone, and your breasts should fill the cups smoothly without spillage or gaps."
  },
  {
    question: "Why do bra sizes vary between different brands?",
    answer: "Different manufacturers use different sizing matrices, fabric elasticity, and wire shapes. Use your calculated size as a primary starting point and refer to brand-specific conversion charts when buying."
  }
];
---

<section id="faq" class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-display-lg mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p class="text-body-lg text-body max-w-2xl">
      Everything you need to know about measuring, bra sizing, and finding your most comfortable fit.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <details class="group bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-md p-6 cursor-pointer hover:border-hairline-strong transition-colors">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-medium text-body-md-strong list-none text-ink">
          <span>{faq.question}</span>
          <span class="transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-mute group-hover:text-ink">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-body text-body-sm pt-4 border-t border-hairline leading-relaxed">
          <p>{faq.answer}</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
